{%- comment -%}
  ElmsNest v2 COLLECTION — the FIRST-OPTION-AXIS PARSER (collection WINNING-SPEC §3.4, §4.2, §4.4, §4.5).

  This snippet is the SINGLE SOURCE OF EVERY NUMBER ON THE COLLECTION PAGE. §6.19 is absolute: no
  length, no quantity, no watt, no price and no per-unit figure is ever typed into a section. They all
  come from here, and here they all come from product.options_with_values[0] and variant.price.

  It reads ONE product's first option axis and prints a parsed model of it: for every option value, the
  number the buyer measures in, the unit that number is in, the real price at that value, the variant
  that price belongs to, and whether it can be bought. Nothing is invented: a value with no number in it
  prints an empty number, and the section carries it in the "לא צוין" bucket (C9, §3.4) rather than
  hiding it (§6.6).

  ------------------------------------------------------------------ call signatures
  A. the model the no-JS markup is built from (default):

      {%- capture env2_axis -%}
        {%- render 'elmsnest-v2-coll-axis', product: product -%}
      {%- endcapture -%}
      {%- assign env2_recs = env2_axis | split: '~~R~~' -%}
      {%- assign env2_meta = env2_recs[0] | split: '~~F~~' -%}
      {%- for env2_rec in env2_recs offset: 1 -%}
        {%- assign s = env2_rec | split: '~~F~~' -%}
        {{ s[3] }} {{ s[5] }} — {{ s[10] }} ₪        {%- comment -%} 5 מ׳ — 89.90 ₪ {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- endfor -%}

     (A snippet's own {% assign %} does NOT leak to its caller — {% render %} has an isolated scope —
     so the model is PRINTED and the caller splits it back into Liquid variables. This is the same
     convention snippets/elmsnest-v2-pdp-variants.liquid already ships on the PDP; keep it.)

  B. one JSON script tag for the eleven-line ruler enhancement (§3.4) and for debugging:

      {%- render 'elmsnest-v2-coll-axis', product: product, emit: 'json' -%}

  ------------------------------------------------------------------ inputs
    product  : required. Blank, or a product with no options / no variants -> prints NOTHING AT ALL
               (not an empty record — nothing, so `capture | split` yields a single empty string and
               the caller's `env2_recs.size > 1` test is false).
    emit     : 'rows' (default) | 'json'
    json_id  : id of the <script> in json mode. Default 'env2-coll-axis-<handle>'.
    per_unit_word : override for the per-unit noun. Blank -> '₪ למטר' for a length axis and
               '₪ ליחידה' for a quantity axis. The path collection prints '₪ לנקודת אור' (§4.2 C2);
               that is a SECTION word choice, so the section passes it, the snippet never guesses it.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------ the parse, against the real data
  Every first-axis value in brief/side-pages/collection/data.json, and what this snippet makes of it:

    "5 מ׳ / 20 נורות"      -> number 5    unit m     unit_label מ׳   number2 20  unit2 led  (נורות)
    "12×2 מ׳ / 780 LED"    -> number 12   unit area  unit_label מ׳   area_h 2    number2 780 unit2 led
    "1.5×1.5 מ׳ / 96 LED"  -> number 1.5  unit area  unit_label מ׳   area_h 1.5  number2 96  unit2 led
    "2 יחידות"             -> number 2    unit qty   unit_label יח׳
    "4 יח׳"  /  "4 'יח"     -> number 4    unit qty   unit_label יח׳   (the live data carries the ASCII
                              apostrophe form "4 'יח" on waterproof-solar-deck-step-lights; both parse)
    "10 נורות"             -> number 10   unit led   unit_label נורות   (a bulb count, NOT a length:
                              solar-firefly-garden-lights is off-scale on the metre rail, §3.4)
    "6W"  /  "10W"         -> number 6    unit w     unit_label W
    "3000K" / "אור חם 3000K" -> number 3000 unit k   unit_label K   (the number need not lead)
    "72 LED / 100W"        -> number 72   unit led   unit_label LED  number2 100 unit2 w
    "יחידה אחת"            -> number ''   unit ''    — a word is not a number. powerful-solar-garden-light
                              and solar-garden-spotlight-52-led both use it, and §3.4 puts the first in
                              the off-scale band precisely because its axis carries no number.
    "לבן" / "שחור" / "דגם A" / "Default Title" / "כחול" / "RGB צבעוני" / "USB" / "זוג"
                           -> number ''   unit ''    — a colour / model / power-source axis. meta[9]
                              (measured) is '0' and the whole product belongs in the price-mode ruler
                              (§3.4: wall and spot have no honest numeric axis at all).

  Unit keys are stable and the sections branch on them, never on the Hebrew:
    m = metres · qty = units · led = bulbs/LED · w = watts · k = kelvin · area = a rectangle in metres
    '' = this value carries no number.

  **area is not a length.** decorative-led-net-lights is sold by area and §4.5 non-negotiable 3 says it
  never appears as a length. meta[9] measured = '0' and meta[10] is_area = '1' for it; a section that
  puts an is_area product on a metre rail has broken the spec. meta[11]/[12] still carry the first
  dimension so the off-scale band can print the span honestly ("מ־1.5×1.5 מ׳ ועד 12×2 מ׳").

  ------------------------------------------------------------------ meta record  (fields ~~F~~, records ~~R~~)
    0  'meta'
    1  handle
    2  axis_name           options_with_values[0].name — 'אורך ומספר נורות', 'כמות', 'צבע גוף', 'Title'
    3  unit                the axis's DOMINANT unit key: the unit of the first value that carries one
    4  unit_label          the printable token: 'מ׳' 'יח׳' 'נורות' 'LED' 'W' 'K' ''
    5  unit_word           the noun for prose: 'מטרים' 'יחידות' 'נורות' 'ואט' 'קלווין' 'שטח' ''
    6  per_unit_label      '₪ למטר' | '₪ ליחידה' | ''  (or the per_unit_word the caller passed)
    7  stops               how many stop records follow (= the axis's value count)
    8  numbered            how many of them carry a number in the dominant unit
    9  measured            '1' when this product belongs on a rail in its own unit; '0' otherwise
                           (no number anywhere, or the axis is an area)
    10 is_area             '1' | '0'
    11 min_number          smallest number on the axis, '' when none
    12 max_number          largest number on the axis, '' when none  ← the "האורך המרבי: 8 מ׳" figure
    13 max_price           the price at max_number, '' when none
    14 price_min           product.price_min          '89.90'
    15 price_max           product.price_max          '179.90'
    16 price_varies        '1' | '0'
    17 variants            product.variants.size
    18 values              the axis's value count (= stops)
    19 available           '1' when any variant is available
    20 default_variant_id  the cheapest AVAILABLE variant (else the first) — the scene card's form
    21 'e'                 terminator. A trailing empty field is dropped by split, so every record ends
                           in a literal 'e' and no real field is ever last.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------ stop record, one per option value
    0  'stop'
    1  i                   0-based, in the option's own value order
    2  value               the raw option value, unescaped ("5 מ׳ / 20 נורות")
    3  number              '5' | '1.5' | ''      the number the buyer measures in
    4  unit                m | qty | led | w | k | area | ''
    5  unit_label          'מ׳' | 'יח׳' | 'נורות' | 'LED' | 'W' | 'K' | ''
    6  area_h              the second dimension of an area value ('2' of 12×2), '' otherwise
    7  number2             the second number in the value ('20' of "5 מ׳ / 20 נורות'), '' when none
    8  unit2               its unit key
    9  unit2_label         its printable token
    10 price               the LOWEST price at this value    '89.90'
    11 price_cents         8990
    12 price_max           the HIGHEST price at this value   '89.90' (wall axes span: 109.90–193.90)
    13 per_unit            price ÷ number, to the agora, ONLY for m and qty; '' otherwise (§4.4 n-n 1)
    14 per_unit_label      '₪ למטר' | '₪ ליחידה' | ''  — the section prefixes '≈', never this snippet
    15 available           '1' when any variant at this value is available
    16 variant_id          the first AVAILABLE variant at this value (else the first) — the row's form
    17 variant_count       how many variants share this value
    18 'e'                 terminator

  Nothing here is escaped. Escape at the point of use ({{ s[2] | escape }}), exactly as the rest of the
  theme does. The json emit escapes through the `json` filter.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------ the JSON shape (emit: 'json')
    <script type="application/json" id="env2-coll-axis-<handle>">
    {"handle":…,"axis":…,"unit":…,"unit_label":…,"unit_word":…,"per_unit_label":…,
     "measured":true,"area":false,"min":5,"max":12,"max_price":…,"price_min":…,"price_max":…,
     "variants":24,"available":true,"default_variant_id":123,
     "stops":[{"i":0,"value":…,"number":5,"unit":"m","unit_label":…,"area_h":null,
               "number2":20,"unit2":"led","unit2_label":…,"price":…,"price_cents":8990,
               "price_max":…,"per_unit":…,"per_unit_label":…,"available":true,
               "variant_id":123,"variants":4}]}
    </script>
  Numbers are JSON numbers; a missing number is null. Prices stay STRINGS ('89.90') because they are
  already formatted to the agora and re-formatting them in JS would reintroduce 1-decimal figures.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign env2_ok = false
  if product != blank and product.variants.size > 0 and product.options_with_values.size > 0
    assign env2_ok = true
  endif
-%}
{%- if env2_ok -%}
{%- liquid
  assign FS = '~~F~~'
  assign RS = '~~R~~'
  assign SEPS = '|/|·|-|־|+|,|×|'
  assign DIGITS = '0123456789.'

  assign opt = product.options_with_values[0]
  assign axis_name = opt.name
  assign nvals = opt.values.size

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- 0. the product-wide numbers
  assign p_min = product.price_min | money_without_currency
  assign p_max = product.price_max | money_without_currency
  assign p_varies = '0'
  if product.price_varies
    assign p_varies = '1'
  endif
  assign any_avail = '0'
  assign def_vid = product.variants[0].id
  assign def_price = 0
  for v in product.variants
    if v.available
      assign any_avail = '1'
      if def_price == 0 or v.price < def_price
        assign def_price = v.price
        assign def_vid = v.id
      endif
    endif
  endfor

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- 1. one record per option value
  assign body = ''
  assign m_unit = ''
  assign m_label = ''
  assign m_numbered = 0
  assign m_area = false
  assign m_min = ''
  assign m_max = ''
  assign m_maxprice = ''

  for value in opt.values
    assign si = forloop.index0

    # -------------------------------------------------------------- 1a. the number parse
    assign s_num = ''
    assign s_rest = ''
    assign s_areah = ''
    assign s_num2 = ''
    assign s_rest2 = ''
    assign is_area = false
    assign toks = value | split: ' '
    for t in toks
      assign numpart = ''
      assign rest = ''
      assign stopped = false
      assign chars = t | split: ''
      for ch in chars
        if stopped
          assign rest = rest | append: ch
        else
          if DIGITS contains ch
            assign numpart = numpart | append: ch
          else
            assign stopped = true
            assign rest = rest | append: ch
          endif
        endif
      endfor
      if numpart != ''
        assign rest_head = rest | slice: 0
        if rest_head == '×' and s_num == ''
          comment
            an area token — "12×2", "1.5×1.5". The first dimension is the number, the second is
            area_h, and the unit token that follows ("מ׳") attaches as the label on the next pass.
          endcomment
          assign is_area = true
          assign s_num = numpart
          assign s_areah = rest | remove_first: '×'
        elsif s_num == ''
          assign s_num = numpart
          assign s_rest = rest
        elsif s_num2 == ''
          assign s_num2 = numpart
          assign s_rest2 = rest
        endif
      else
        assign sep_probe = '|' | append: t | append: '|'
        unless SEPS contains sep_probe
          if s_num != '' and s_rest == '' and s_num2 == ''
            assign s_rest = t
          elsif s_num2 != '' and s_rest2 == ''
            assign s_rest2 = t
          endif
        endunless
      endif
    endfor

    # -------------------------------------------------------------- 1b. unit 1, normalised
    assign s_unit = ''
    assign s_label = ''
    if s_num != ''
      if is_area
        assign s_unit = 'area'
        assign s_label = s_rest | default: 'מ׳'
      elsif s_rest contains 'מ׳' or s_rest == 'מ' or s_rest contains 'מטר'
        assign s_unit = 'm'
        assign s_label = 'מ׳'
      elsif s_rest contains 'יח'
        assign s_unit = 'qty'
        assign s_label = 'יח׳'
      elsif s_rest contains 'נור'
        assign s_unit = 'led'
        assign s_label = 'נורות'
      elsif s_rest contains 'LED' or s_rest contains 'led'
        assign s_unit = 'led'
        assign s_label = 'LED'
      elsif s_rest == 'W' or s_rest == 'w' or s_rest contains 'ואט'
        assign s_unit = 'w'
        assign s_label = 'W'
      elsif s_rest == 'K' or s_rest == 'k' or s_rest contains 'קלווין'
        assign s_unit = 'k'
        assign s_label = 'K'
      else
        assign s_label = s_rest
      endif
    endif

    # -------------------------------------------------------------- 1c. unit 2, normalised
    assign s_unit2 = ''
    assign s_label2 = ''
    if s_num2 != ''
      if s_rest2 contains 'מ׳' or s_rest2 == 'מ' or s_rest2 contains 'מטר'
        assign s_unit2 = 'm'
        assign s_label2 = 'מ׳'
      elsif s_rest2 contains 'יח'
        assign s_unit2 = 'qty'
        assign s_label2 = 'יח׳'
      elsif s_rest2 contains 'נור'
        assign s_unit2 = 'led'
        assign s_label2 = 'נורות'
      elsif s_rest2 contains 'LED' or s_rest2 contains 'led'
        assign s_unit2 = 'led'
        assign s_label2 = 'LED'
      elsif s_rest2 == 'W' or s_rest2 == 'w' or s_rest2 contains 'ואט'
        assign s_unit2 = 'w'
        assign s_label2 = 'W'
      elsif s_rest2 == 'K' or s_rest2 == 'k' or s_rest2 contains 'קלווין'
        assign s_unit2 = 'k'
        assign s_label2 = 'K'
      else
        assign s_label2 = s_rest2
      endif
    endif

    # -------------------------------------------------------------- 1d. the real prices at this value
    assign s_lo = 0
    assign s_hi = 0
    assign s_vid = 0
    assign s_avail = '0'
    assign s_count = 0
    for v in product.variants
      if v.options[0] == value
        assign s_count = s_count | plus: 1
        if s_lo == 0 or v.price < s_lo
          assign s_lo = v.price
        endif
        if v.price > s_hi
          assign s_hi = v.price
        endif
        if s_vid == 0
          assign s_vid = v.id
        endif
        if v.available
          assign s_avail = '1'
          if v.price == s_lo
            assign s_vid = v.id
          endif
        endif
      endif
    endfor
    assign s_price = s_lo | money_without_currency
    assign s_pricemax = s_hi | money_without_currency

    # -------------------------------------------------------------- 1e. the derived per-unit figure (C2)
    assign s_per = ''
    assign s_perlabel = ''
    if s_num != '' and s_count > 0
      assign nnum = s_num | plus: 0.0
      if nnum > 0
        if s_unit == 'm'
          assign s_per = s_lo | divided_by: nnum | round | money_without_currency
          assign s_perlabel = per_unit_word | default: '₪ למטר'
        elsif s_unit == 'qty'
          assign s_per = s_lo | divided_by: nnum | round | money_without_currency
          assign s_perlabel = per_unit_word | default: '₪ ליחידה'
        endif
      endif
    endif

    # -------------------------------------------------------------- 1f. roll the axis-wide meta
    if s_unit != '' and m_unit == ''
      assign m_unit = s_unit
      assign m_label = s_label
    endif
    if is_area
      assign m_area = true
    endif
    if s_num != '' and s_unit == m_unit
      assign m_numbered = m_numbered | plus: 1
      assign cur = s_num | plus: 0.0
      if m_min == ''
        assign m_min = s_num
        assign m_max = s_num
        assign m_maxprice = s_price
      else
        assign lo = m_min | plus: 0.0
        assign hi = m_max | plus: 0.0
        if cur < lo
          assign m_min = s_num
        endif
        if cur > hi
          assign m_max = s_num
          assign m_maxprice = s_price
        endif
      endif
    endif

    assign rec = 'stop' | append: FS | append: si | append: FS | append: value | append: FS | append: s_num
    assign rec = rec | append: FS | append: s_unit | append: FS | append: s_label | append: FS | append: s_areah
    assign rec = rec | append: FS | append: s_num2 | append: FS | append: s_unit2 | append: FS | append: s_label2
    assign rec = rec | append: FS | append: s_price | append: FS | append: s_lo | append: FS | append: s_pricemax
    assign rec = rec | append: FS | append: s_per | append: FS | append: s_perlabel | append: FS | append: s_avail
    assign rec = rec | append: FS | append: s_vid | append: FS | append: s_count | append: FS | append: 'e'
    assign body = body | append: RS | append: rec
  endfor

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- 2. the axis-wide words
  assign m_word = ''
  assign m_perlabel = ''
  if m_unit == 'm'
    assign m_word = 'מטרים'
    assign m_perlabel = per_unit_word | default: '₪ למטר'
  elsif m_unit == 'qty'
    assign m_word = 'יחידות'
    assign m_perlabel = per_unit_word | default: '₪ ליחידה'
  elsif m_unit == 'led'
    assign m_word = 'נורות'
  elsif m_unit == 'w'
    assign m_word = 'ואט'
  elsif m_unit == 'k'
    assign m_word = 'קלווין'
  elsif m_unit == 'area'
    assign m_word = 'שטח'
  endif

  assign m_measured = '0'
  if m_numbered > 0 and m_area == false and m_unit != ''
    assign m_measured = '1'
  endif
  assign m_isarea = '0'
  if m_area
    assign m_isarea = '1'
  endif

  assign meta = 'meta' | append: FS | append: product.handle | append: FS | append: axis_name
  assign meta = meta | append: FS | append: m_unit | append: FS | append: m_label | append: FS | append: m_word
  assign meta = meta | append: FS | append: m_perlabel | append: FS | append: nvals | append: FS | append: m_numbered
  assign meta = meta | append: FS | append: m_measured | append: FS | append: m_isarea
  assign meta = meta | append: FS | append: m_min | append: FS | append: m_max | append: FS | append: m_maxprice
  assign meta = meta | append: FS | append: p_min | append: FS | append: p_max | append: FS | append: p_varies
  assign meta = meta | append: FS | append: product.variants.size | append: FS | append: nvals
  assign meta = meta | append: FS | append: any_avail | append: FS | append: def_vid | append: FS | append: 'e'

  assign env2_mode = emit | default: 'rows'
-%}
{%- if env2_mode == 'json' -%}
{%- liquid
  assign jid = json_id | default: 'env2-coll-axis-'
  if json_id == blank
    assign jid = jid | append: product.handle
  endif
  # body opens with a record separator, so strip it before splitting or the first element is empty
  assign recs = body | remove_first: RS | split: RS
  assign t_yes = 'true'
  assign t_no = 'false'
  assign j_measured = t_no
  if m_measured == '1'
    assign j_measured = t_yes
  endif
  assign j_area = t_no
  if m_area
    assign j_area = t_yes
  endif
  assign j_avail = t_no
  if any_avail == '1'
    assign j_avail = t_yes
  endif
  assign NUL = 'null'
  assign j_min = m_min | default: NUL
  assign j_max = m_max | default: NUL
-%}
<script type="application/json" id="{{ jid }}">
{"handle":{{ product.handle | json }},"axis":{{ axis_name | json }},"unit":{{ m_unit | json }},"unit_label":{{ m_label | json }},"unit_word":{{ m_word | json }},"per_unit_label":{{ m_perlabel | json }},"measured":{{ j_measured }},"area":{{ j_area }},"min":{{ j_min }},"max":{{ j_max }},"max_price":{{ m_maxprice | json }},"price_min":{{ p_min | json }},"price_max":{{ p_max | json }},"variants":{{ product.variants.size }},"available":{{ j_avail }},"default_variant_id":{{ def_vid }},"stops":[
{%- for rec in recs -%}
  {%- assign s = rec | split: FS -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign sn = s[3] | default: NUL
    assign sah = s[6] | default: NUL
    assign sn2 = s[7] | default: NUL
    assign sper = s[13]
    assign sav = t_no
    if s[15] == '1'
      assign sav = t_yes
    endif
  -%}
  {%- unless forloop.first %},{% endunless -%}
  {"i":{{ s[1] }},"value":{{ s[2] | json }},"number":{{ sn }},"unit":{{ s[4] | json }},"unit_label":{{ s[5] | json }},"area_h":{{ sah }},"number2":{{ sn2 }},"unit2":{{ s[8] | json }},"unit2_label":{{ s[9] | json }},"price":{{ s[10] | json }},"price_cents":{{ s[11] }},"price_max":{{ s[12] | json }},"per_unit":{% if sper == blank %}{{ NUL }}{% else %}{{ sper | json }}{% endif %},"per_unit_label":{{ s[14] | json }},"available":{{ sav }},"variant_id":{{ s[16] }},"variants":{{ s[17] }}}
{%- endfor -%}
]}
</script>
{%- else -%}
{{- meta }}{{ body -}}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
